# Repository-root environment file.
#
# The API and the web app do not load this file.
# install.sh copies it to ./.env, and nothing in the backend, frontend, or
# contract Makefile reads that copy.
#
# Copy the files the processes actually read:
#   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#
# The backend loads backend/.env (dotenv, working directory backend/).
# Vite loads frontend/.env at build time.
# `make -C contracts deploy-testnet` and `make -C contracts init-contract`
# read STELLAR_SECRET_KEY, CONTRACT_ID, STELLAR_NETWORK, and REFLECTOR_ADDRESS
# from the shell, not from this file.
#
# Names that used to be set here, and what the code reads instead:
#
#   NETWORK_PASSPHRASE
#     Not read. Deploy scripts use SOROBAN_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE.
#   RPC_URL
#     Not read. The backend uses SOROBAN_RPC_URL, then STELLAR_RPC_URL.
#     Unset testnet default: https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
#     Unset mainnet default: https://soroban-rpc.mainnet.stellar.gateway.fm
#   NETWORK
#     Not read. The backend and `make init-contract` use STELLAR_NETWORK
#     (default testnet).
#   CONTRACT_ID
#     Not read by the API. The API uses STELLAR_CONTRACT_ADDRESS or
#     CONTRACT_ADDRESS. `make init-contract` reads CONTRACT_ID from the shell.
#   USER_PRIVATE_KEY
#     Not read. Signing uses STELLAR_REBALANCE_SECRET or STELLAR_SECRET_KEY.
#     `make deploy-testnet` reads STELLAR_SECRET_KEY from the shell.
#   PORT=3002
#     Wrong port. The API default is 3001. Set PORT in backend/.env.
#   DATABASE_URL=sqlite:./data/portfolio.db
#     The sqlite: scheme is not parsed. Local SQLite uses DB_PATH
#     (default ./data/portfolio.db). DATABASE_URL is a Postgres URI when set.
#   REDIS_URL, RATE_LIMIT_MAX, NODE_ENV
#     These names are real backend settings. Set them in backend/.env.
#     REDIS_URL falls back to redis://localhost:6379. RATE_LIMIT_MAX falls
#     back to 100. NODE_ENV falls back to development.
